night Wednesday even after\nrainfall has ended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-01T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0131f538810dac521ad09e37656bcfc83b15cbff.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0131f538810dac521ad09e37656bcfc83b15cbff.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-30T11:21:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 301121 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 521 AM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to widespread precipitation showers and storms continue through Wednesday evening. - Flooding concerns are increased for rain-soaked terrain, especially within and adjacent to the southern San Juans. - A Flood Watch is in effect for southeast Uta","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-30T07:02:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Moisture will continue to wrap into southern and central portions of the area today as this system moves through. Tropical moisture remains in place and moderate to heavy rain showers will continue to be a threat with high probability of wetting rainfall. Warmer and drier conditions move in by tomorrow and persist through the remainder of the forecast. Critical fire weather condition","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"pgs01","station_name":"Pagosa Springs","distance_km":2.6,"soil_temp_5cm_f":57.81,"soil_temp_15cm_f":57.24,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":272.67,"wind_speed_mph":8.43,"air_temp_f":54.03,"relative_humidity":0.809,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/pgs01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KPSO","distance_km":0,"raw_me